[size=6][b]S2MM – Stalker 2 Mod Manager[/b][/size]
[size=3]Install, sort and conflict-check your mods – edit MCM settings and key bindings – follow yourself on a live map.[/size]

[b]Windows & Linux · Setup & Portable · English & German · Free and open source (MIT)[/b]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LizenzFracht/Stalker2ModManager/master/docs/media/01-mods.png[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=5][b]What it does[/b][/size]

[b]All mod formats in one place[/b]
Drag & drop ZIP, 7z or RAR archives, loose .pak/.utoc/.ucas files, DLL/ASI plugins or folders. S2MM figures out where everything belongs:
[list]
[*]classic pak mods → [i]~mods[/i] (with load-order prefix and [i]_P[/i] suffix)
[*]official Zone Kit mods → [i]Stalker2\Mods\<Name>[/i] (e.g. the Mod Configuration Menu)
[*]UE4SS Lua mods → [i]Binaries\Win64\ue4ss\Mods[/i]
[*]DLL/ASI plugins and UE4SS itself → [i]Binaries\Win64[/i]
[/list]
Mods with a [b]FOMOD installer[/b] or several [b]variant folders[/b] get an options dialog – and you can change your choice later without reinstalling.

[b]Load order, conflicts and auto-sort[/b]
Drag mods into order – the lower one wins. S2MM reads the content of every pak and IoStore container and shows [b]exactly which .cfg or asset[/b] one mod overrides in another. [i]Auto-sort[/i] suggests a sensible order and explains every move.

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LizenzFracht/Stalker2ModManager/master/docs/media/reorder.gif[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LizenzFracht/Stalker2ModManager/master/docs/media/03-conflicts.png[/img][/center]

[b]Safe by design[/b]
[list]
[*]Mods stay in their own library and are hard-linked (or copied) into the game.
[*]Only files S2MM placed are ever removed; game files a mod replaces are backed up and restored.
[*][b]Restore vanilla[/b] (offered on first start): removes all mods and – if you want – a manually installed UE4SS, other mods and all Engine.ini tweaks. Nothing is deleted, everything goes into a dated backup folder.
[*]A read-only [b]Vanilla[/b] profile plus as many own profiles as you like.
[/list]

[b]Mod settings (MCM) and key bindings[/b]
[list]
[*]Edit the settings of the [b]Mod Configuration Menu[/b] without starting the game.
[*]See every key your mods bind (UE4SS scripts, config files, MCM), spot double bindings and rebind with a key press.
[*]Edit a mod's .ini, .lua or .json config right in the app.
[/list]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LizenzFracht/Stalker2ModManager/master/docs/media/04-keybindings.png[/img][/center]

[b]Live map[/b]
S2MM opens [url=https://github.com/joric/stalker]joric's interactive Stalker 2 map[/url] in your browser and shows your in-game position and viewing direction live – with follow mode and a layer filter. A tiny bundled UE4SS mod reports your position; the map server only runs on your own PC.

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LizenzFracht/Stalker2ModManager/master/docs/media/live-map.gif[/img][/center]

[b]Game tweaks[/b]
Curated Engine.ini switches (chromatic aberration, vignette, film grain, depth of field, motion blur, sharpening, texture pool, shader cache, view distance …), your own CVars, import/export of Engine.ini files and one-click restore.

[b]And more[/b]
[list]
[*]Installs [b]UE4SS on demand[/b] – current release from GitHub incl. the Stalker 2 config for Steam or Game Pass, toggleable like a mod.
[*]Finds Steam, Game Pass/Xbox, GOG and Epic installs and warns after game updates.
[*]English and German interface, following your system language.
[*]Portable mode – all data stays next to the program.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]Downloads[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Windows setup[/b] – S2MM_x.y.z_windows_x64_setup.exe
[*][b]Windows portable[/b] – S2MM_x.y.z_windows_x64_portable.zip (unzip, run S2MM.exe)
[*][b]Linux setup[/b] – S2MM_x.y.z_linux_amd64_setup.deb
[*][b]Linux portable[/b] – S2MM_x.y.z_linux_x86_64_portable.AppImage (chmod +x, run)
[/list]
Windows may show a SmartScreen warning because the program is not code-signed ("More info → Run anyway"). The source code is on [url=https://github.com/LizenzFracht/Stalker2ModManager]GitHub[/url] if you prefer to build it yourself.

[b]Linux:[/b] S2MM manages a Steam/Proton install. For UE4SS mods add [i]WINEDLLOVERRIDES="dwmapi=n,b" %command%[/i] to the game's launch options.

[b]Nexus downloads:[/b] the built-in "Mod Manager Download" support is switched off until S2MM is registered with Nexus Mods. Download mods in your browser and drop the archive into S2MM – the mod ID and version are read from the file name.

[line]

[size=5][b]Quick start[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Start S2MM – it finds your game automatically.
[*]Optional: click [i]Restore vanilla[/i] in the welcome dialog for a clean start.
[*]Drop your mod archives into the window and choose options where asked.
[*]Sort, check the [i]Conflicts[/i] page, then click [b]Apply[/b] and [b]Launch game[/b].
[/list]

[line]

